{"formatVersion":1,"kind":"rules","rows":[{"antecedent_key":"pegmatite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"lithium","expected_minerals":["spodumene","lepidolite","petalite","tourmaline"],"id":"0116bd6f-0df4-4a91-931f-2c865fbe1b80","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Highly evolved (LCT) pegmatites concentrate lithium in spodumene and lepidolite, making zoned pegmatites a prime lithium target.","requires_setting":["craton_margin","collisional_orogen"],"weight":0.38},{"antecedent_key":"pegmatite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"beryllium","expected_minerals":["beryl","aquamarine"],"id":"12eb0a1d-417c-4a6f-a6e5-9c03f523aa4d","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Beryllium crystallises as beryl (including aquamarine) in pegmatites, a classic rare-metal and gem indicator.","requires_setting":["craton_margin"],"weight":0.35},{"antecedent_key":"laterite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"nickel","expected_minerals":["garnierite","goethite"],"id":"26809be6-1e2c-46ef-af06-d3419c7a61f7","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"Deep tropical weathering of ultramafic rock forms nickel laterite, with green garnierite marking the richest zones.","requires_setting":["tropical_weathering"],"weight":0.32},{"antecedent_key":"carbonatite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"niobium","expected_minerals":["pyrochlore","apatite"],"id":"35f0bbd6-7850-4d37-ae6f-5c69ddd9b1e9","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Carbonatites also host most of the world's niobium as pyrochlore, alongside phosphate and fluorite.","requires_setting":["intracontinental_rift"],"weight":0.4},{"antecedent_key":"granite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"lithium","expected_minerals":["spodumene","lepidolite"],"id":"519a00d0-914b-4047-b85e-9111797eae67","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"Some fractionated granites grade into lithium-tantalum pegmatites — worth checking the granite margins.","requires_setting":["craton_margin"],"weight":0.28},{"antecedent_key":"serpentinite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"pgm","expected_minerals":["chromite","platinum"],"id":"68519cb7-9cd8-402c-800d-dcbf964d4fa3","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"Ultramafic bodies and their chromitites are a recognised setting for platinum-group metals.","requires_setting":["craton"],"weight":0.32},{"antecedent_key":"granite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"tin","expected_minerals":["cassiterite","tourmaline","topaz"],"id":"6b05cdf6-25ee-4e18-9468-3385054d5be6","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"Evolved (S-type) granites can concentrate tin, tungsten and rare metals in their cupolas and greisen zones.","requires_setting":["collisional_orogen"],"weight":0.3},{"antecedent_key":"kimberlite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":null,"expected_minerals":["pyrope garnet","chrome diopside","chromite","ilmenite"],"id":"7443daa6-430a-4ceb-bab8-fa1eed1e52e7","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Mantle indicator minerals (pyrope garnet, chrome diopside, chromite, ilmenite) survive in the soil around kimberlite and are what geologists pan for to trace a pipe.","requires_setting":["craton"],"weight":0.4},{"antecedent_key":"pegmatite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"tantalum","expected_minerals":["tantalite","columbite","cassiterite"],"id":"78657617-6574-46f9-829d-fe550c68b36d","likelihood":"common","relationship":"The same evolved pegmatites that carry lithium often host tantalum-niobium oxides (columbite-tantalite) and tin.","requires_setting":["craton_margin"],"weight":0.36},{"antecedent_key":"kimberlite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"diamond","expected_minerals":["diamond","pyrope garnet","chrome diopside","chromite","ilmenite","olivine"],"id":"815944e9-86a2-47f2-b32d-5e7c8c8678dc","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Kimberlite is a deep-mantle volcanic rock that can carry diamond and mantle indicator minerals to surface, which is why it is the world's primary diamond source.","requires_setting":["craton","precambrian_basement"],"weight":0.4},{"antecedent_key":"gabbro","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"vanadium","expected_minerals":["titanomagnetite","magnetite"],"id":"82c8abc3-e905-455b-908b-ebc4af7eb51b","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"Titaniferous magnetite layers in mafic intrusions carry vanadium and titanium.","requires_setting":["large_igneous_province"],"weight":0.3},{"antecedent_key":"skarn","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"copper","expected_minerals":["chalcopyrite","bornite","garnet","magnetite"],"id":"83ec51ff-82cf-4c2c-a774-99952e3989e4","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Skarns around fertile intrusions frequently carry copper (and iron), making the intrusive contact a key place to sample.","requires_setting":["continental_arc"],"weight":0.36},{"antecedent_key":"greisen","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"tungsten","expected_minerals":["wolframite","scheelite","quartz"],"id":"850d0588-188c-45d0-b217-1de41072afd3","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Tungsten (wolframite/scheelite) is commonly enriched with tin in greisen-veined granite cupolas.","requires_setting":["collisional_orogen"],"weight":0.36},{"antecedent_key":"serpentinite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"nickel","expected_minerals":["pentlandite","garnierite","magnetite"],"id":"8abec9b9-9923-499b-94e4-31913a3f01e1","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"Serpentinised ultramafic rock can host nickel — as magmatic sulphide at depth or green garnierite in tropical laterite above it.","requires_setting":["ophiolite","craton"],"weight":0.34},{"antecedent_key":"skarn","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"tungsten","expected_minerals":["scheelite","garnet","pyroxene"],"id":"9a4b6e4a-3758-481e-88ce-a6cfca7c873d","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Where intrusions bake carbonate rocks, calc-silicate skarns form and can concentrate tungsten (scheelite), which fluoresces blue under UV.","requires_setting":["continental_arc"],"weight":0.38},{"antecedent_key":"banded iron formation","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"iron","expected_minerals":["hematite","magnetite","goethite"],"id":"9e5292ac-90ab-440b-a2ca-2d9c3664379d","likelihood":"diagnostic","relationship":"Banded iron formation (BIF) is the world's main iron source; supergene weathering upgrades it to high-grade hematite ore.","requires_setting":["craton"],"weight":0.45},{"antecedent_key":"marble","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"graphite","expected_minerals":["graphite","calcite"],"id":"aa9a4e85-e8c8-4a0e-9fe7-a6c946468a5a","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"High-grade metamorphosed carbonates and associated gneisses can host flake graphite.","requires_setting":["high_grade_metamorphic"],"weight":0.3},{"antecedent_key":"banded iron formation","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"gold","expected_minerals":["pyrite","quartz","arsenopyrite"],"id":"ab03a77b-e422-41e4-80a0-189038acb2c7","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"In some greenstone belts, BIF units are chemically favourable traps that host orogenic gold along structures.","requires_setting":["greenstone_belt"],"weight":0.33},{"antecedent_key":"gabbro","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"pgm","expected_minerals":["chromite","pentlandite","chalcopyrite"],"id":"b408a623-81b9-49b3-81d4-c6d9b88ca270","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"Layered mafic intrusions (gabbro) host reef-style platinum-group-metal and nickel-copper sulphide mineralisation.","requires_setting":["craton","large_igneous_province"],"weight":0.32},{"antecedent_key":"marble","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"corundum","expected_minerals":["corundum","spinel","graphite"],"id":"b47f3cfe-5789-481f-b2f8-6945091c312f","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"Marble can host ruby (corundum) where aluminous, chromium-bearing fluids interacted during metamorphism.","requires_setting":["collisional_orogen"],"weight":0.3},{"antecedent_key":"laterite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"cobalt","expected_minerals":["asbolane","goethite"],"id":"bacefd17-6ea3-4306-a796-91828ebc73cb","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"Nickel laterites commonly carry cobalt in their manganese-oxide layers.","requires_setting":["tropical_weathering"],"weight":0.3},{"antecedent_key":"ultramafic","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"chromium","expected_minerals":["chromite"],"id":"bc3dc6d2-47c4-4bc5-abb9-9bf2b67825b0","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Chromite layers in ultramafic rocks are the main source of chromium and a pathfinder for PGE.","requires_setting":["ophiolite","craton"],"weight":0.34},{"antecedent_key":"carbonatite","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"ree","expected_minerals":["bastnaesite","monazite","apatite","fluorite"],"id":"ccf056d8-2f8c-433c-b08c-4ef1190c50fe","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Carbonatites are the dominant source of rare earth elements, concentrated in bastnaesite, monazite and apatite within the complex.","requires_setting":["intracontinental_rift"],"weight":0.42},{"antecedent_key":"skarn","antecedent_type":"deposit_type","commodity_code":"iron","expected_minerals":["magnetite","hematite","garnet"],"id":"eb0e850f-3578-4d49-a64c-f9e0988b8d80","likelihood":"possible","relationship":"Iron-rich skarns (magnetite) form at intrusive-carbonate contacts and are a recognised iron source.","requires_setting":[],"weight":0.33},{"antecedent_key":"greisen","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"tin","expected_minerals":["cassiterite","wolframite","topaz","tourmaline"],"id":"ef2a4cdc-dddf-467f-8fbc-427ca0126599","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Greisen is altered granite where hot fluids concentrated tin (cassiterite) and tungsten (wolframite) — a classic Sn-W setting.","requires_setting":["collisional_orogen"],"weight":0.38},{"antecedent_key":"quartz vein","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"gold","expected_minerals":["pyrite","arsenopyrite","quartz","visible gold"],"id":"fd7b95fd-14ec-4367-bc94-c63cb4cbe2a6","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Quartz veins within shear zones are the classic setting for orogenic gold, especially where sulphides like pyrite and arsenopyrite are present.","requires_setting":["greenstone_belt","accretionary_orogen"],"weight":0.36},{"antecedent_key":"ultramafic","antecedent_type":"host_rock","commodity_code":"nickel","expected_minerals":["pentlandite","pyrrhotite","chromite"],"id":"ffe55be0-069b-45f6-a75b-b262c9e1b36e","likelihood":"common","relationship":"Ultramafic rocks (komatiite, dunite, peridotite) are the primary hosts for magmatic nickel-copper-PGE sulphide systems.","requires_setting":["craton","large_igneous_province"],"weight":0.36}]}